@startuml
title Allpatek | Parcels and On-demand Weather
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam dpi 140
hide footbox
actor Farmer
participant "Angular SPA" as Web
database "Mock API" as Mock
participant "Open-Meteo" as Weather

Farmer -> Web : Select demo farmer role
Farmer -> Web : Open /parcels/new and fill in details
note right of Web
  Choose coordinates manually, by department or GPS.
  Add crops and optional photos.
end note
Web -> Mock : POST /parcels (status available)
Mock --> Web : Saved parcel
Web --> Farmer : Return to /parcels on success
Farmer -> Web : Open /alerts
Web -> Mock : Read parcel references
Mock --> Web : Parcels
Web -> Web : Keep owner's parcels with valid coordinates
alt Coordinates available
  Web -> Weather : GET forecasts for the owner's parcels
  Weather --> Web : Current, hourly and daily forecast
  Web --> Farmer : Show readings and estimated risk
else No usable coordinates
  Web --> Farmer : No readings
end
note over Web,Weather
  The browser calls Open-Meteo directly.
  The separate Spring GET /api/v1/alerts reads MySQL parcels
  and calls Open-Meteo independently; Angular does not call it.
end note
@enduml
